-- Broadcasting Act (Amendment of First Schedule) Notification 2012 (S 549/2012).
--
-- Source: subjects/sg/broadcasting-amendment-of-first-schedule-notification-2012/registers/source-bundle/
-- BA1994-S549-2012.txt, quoted by plain `src:N`.
--
-- This module has NO time built-ins.  It records the Notification's dates and the Schedule it substitutes.
-- Which reader sees it, and for which conduct, is decided in sgbau-first-schedule.l4.
--
-- THE THREE DATES, and which one governs what:
--   made: 30 October 2012 (the signature line);
--   first published: 31 October 2012, 5.00 pm (the front matter);
--   deemed in operation from: 1 January 2011 (cl 1).
-- The last is the DATE THE TEXT APPLIES FROM, and it is earlier than the other two.  The first publication is the
-- day a reader could first have known the text, and that is the day the reader gate in sgbau-first-schedule.l4
-- uses.  The day it was made is not used: a Notification nobody has seen cannot be read.  (Whether the general law
-- of subsidiary legislation treats a Notification as effective before publication is not in the sources.)
-- A DATE has no time of day, so the 5.00 pm is not representable (finding 5 in NOTES.md).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgbau-nouns`

§ `Citation and commencement (cl 1)`

-- src:20 | 1. This Notification may be cited as the Broadcasting Act
-- src:21 | (Amendment of First Schedule) Notification 2012 and shall be deemed
-- src:22 | to have come into operation on 1st January 2011.
@ref S 549/2012, cl 1 (src:20-22)
`S 549/2012 is deemed to have come into operation on` MEANS Date 1 1 2011

§ `When it was published and made`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 31st October 2012 at 5.00 pm.
@ref S 549/2012, front matter (src:3)
`S 549/2012 was first published in the Gazette on` MEANS Date 31 10 2012

-- src:37 | Made this 30th day of October 2012.
@ref S 549/2012, signature line (src:37)
`S 549/2012 was made on` MEANS Date 30 10 2012

§ `The First Schedule substituted by cl 2`

-- Cl 2 deletes the First Schedule and substitutes a Schedule of one item, the TVRO system, with the same
-- definition the three-item Schedule gave it.  Items 1 and 2 and their definitions are gone.
-- src:25 | 2. The First Schedule to the Broadcasting Act is deleted and
-- src:26 | the following Schedule substituted therefor:
-- src:27 | ‘‘FIRST SCHEDULE
-- src:28 | Section 2(1)
-- src:29 | BROADCASTING APPARATUS
-- src:31 | 1. Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system).
-- src:32 | In this Schedule, ‘‘television receive-only satellite receiving system’’ means
-- src:33 | any apparatus (including a dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus
-- src:34 | capable of direct reception of any broadcasting service emitted from or passing
-- src:35 | through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial space.’’.
@ref S 549/2012, cl 2 (src:25-35)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the TVRO-only Schedule specifies the apparatus` MEANS
    apparatus's `capable of direct reception from a satellite in extra-terrestrial space`
